Article 5 (Matters to Be Stated in Audit Reports) An auditor shall state the following matters in an audit report under Article 39 of the Act and shall sign and affix a seal thereto:
1. An outline of the auditing methods;
2. Where matters required to be entered in accounting books are omitted or inadequately stated, or where entries in a balance sheet or income statement do not agree with those in accounting books, a statement to that effect;
3. Whether the settlement documents accurately present the assets and financial performance of the ship investment company in accordance with statutes and the articles of incorporation;
4. Whether changes in accounting policies for preparing settlement documents are appropriate;
5. Where directors have committed misconduct in performing their duties or material violations of statutes or the articles of incorporation, the facts thereof;
6. Where there were obstacles to investigations necessary for the audit, a statement to that effect.
